{"base_rate":0.32978723404255317,"brier":0.2320219858156028,"bss":-0.04974207202594294,"bss_hi":0.07514084170759924,"bss_lo":-0.17924454912930776,"chart":{"base":[347.1,260.7],"fp":[432.7,78.0],"note":{"base":"skill -0.05 — higher than 9% of cities","fp":"low end +14pp, high end +34pp","rel":"promised 1% → rained 6%; promised 93% → rained 56%"},"rel":"67.6,439 88.2,397.8 129.4,314.2 295.2,242.4 649.2,225.2"},"country":"BS","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve"],"ece":0.1870567375886525,"ess":367.4531327492155,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Nassau</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Nassau rain forecast is cannot beat its own climatology, though 9 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (100%), believe about\n<b>62%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>2%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 564 days, 2024-05-03 to\n2026-05-26. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nNASSAU 4.2 SSW, 2.0 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score -0.05, ranked 197 of\n216 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(180&ndash;204) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>2%</b></td><td class='num'>46</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>2%</td><td class='num'><b>9%</b></td><td class='num'>66</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>3%</td><td class='num'><b>15%</b></td><td class='num'>39</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>5%</td><td class='num'><b>16%</b></td><td class='num'>75</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>8%</td><td class='num'><b>29%</b></td><td class='num'>45</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>13%</td><td class='num'><b>39%</b></td><td class='num'>66</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>23%</td><td class='num'><b>44%</b></td><td class='num'>57</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>51%</td><td class='num'><b>60%</b></td><td class='num'>57</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>86%</td><td class='num'><b>49%</b></td><td class='num'>55</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>100%</td><td class='num'><b>62%</b></td><td class='num'>58</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">9 of 10 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Nassau</b> <span class=\"muted\">Bahamas</span></p>\n  <div class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag bad\">Cannot beat climatology</span><details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What does this label mean?\" title=\"What does this label mean?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>Compared with a simple guess: saying &ldquo;33% chance of rain&rdquo; every day, because it rains here on 33% of days.</p><p>The forecast did worse than that guess. The difference is within the margin of error.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details>\n    <span class=\"muted\">9 points off by more than chance</span></div>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score<details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What is the skill score?\" title=\"What is the skill score?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>How much better the forecast is than that simple guess. 0 means no better, 1 means perfect, below 0 means worse. Day-ahead rain forecasts usually score 0.3 to 0.5.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details></dt><dd>-0.05</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>180&ndash;204\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 216</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>564 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Nassau &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Nassau\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" f