10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"239.16105263157894\" cy=\"164.87719298245617\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 86%&amp;#10;It rained 49% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 55 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"362.8261818181819\" cy=\"203.3090909090909\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 100%&amp;#10;It rained 62% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 58 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"411.8168965517241\" cy=\"156.06896551724137\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(33%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p class=\"muted\">Not enough days in this city's record to split the year into four and still say anything defensible about each part. The split is shown only where it is supported.</p>\n"},"lat":25.05823,"lon":-77.34306,"n":564,"n_cities":216,"name":"Nassau","offset_days":-1,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.01,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0,"n":46,"obs":0.021739130434782608,"sig":true},{"hi":0.03,"lo":0.01,"mean":0.015151515151515152,"n":66,"obs":0.09090909090909091,"sig":true},{"hi":0.04,"lo":0.03,"mean":0.030000000000000002,"n":39,"obs":0.15384615384615385,"sig":true},{"hi":0.06200000000000017,"lo":0.04,"mean":0.04773333333333333,"n":75,"obs":0.16,"sig":true},{"hi":0